<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xmlns:mstts="https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts" xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-NovaTurboMultilingualNeural">
    <mstts:express-as style="conversational">
      <prosody rate="0.95" pitch="medium">
        <mstts:silence type="Leading" value="800ms"/>
        <emphasis level="strong">The rich don't work for money.</emphasis>
        <break time="500ms" strength="medium"/>
        This <emphasis level="moderate">fundamental principle</emphasis> is what truly separates the wealthy from everyone else. 
        <break time="500ms" strength="medium"/>
        While most people spend their lives chasing a paycheck, <prosody contour="(10 percent,+20 percent) (50 percent,-10 percent)">the rich know that real wealth comes from making money work for them.</prosody>
        <break time="500ms" strength="medium"/>
        Instead of trading their time for money, they focus on <emphasis level="moderate">acquiring assets</emphasis> that generate <emphasis level="strong">passive income</emphasis>.
        <break time="500ms" strength="medium"/>
        Think about it—what if your money worked harder than you did?
        <break time="500ms" strength="medium"/>
        This shift in <emphasis level="moderate">mindset</emphasis> is absolutely crucial for anyone aiming for <emphasis level="strong">financial freedom</emphasis>.
        <mstts:silence type="Tailing" value="1200ms"/>
      </prosody>
    </mstts:express-as>
  </voice>
</speak>